{
  "title": "58: Al-Mujadilah المجادلة",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful\nقَدْ سَمِعَ اللّٰهُ قَوْلَ الَّتِىْ تُجَادِلُكَ فِىْ زَوْجِهَا وَ تَشْتَكِىْۤ اِلَى اللّٰهِ ۖ وَاللّٰهُ يَسْمَعُ تَحَاوُرَكُمَا ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ سَمِيْعٌ ۢ بَصِيْرٌ‏(1)\nQAD SAME-A’L LAAHO QAWLAL LATEE TOJAADELOKA FEE ZAWJEHAA WA TASHTAKEE ELAL LAAH, WAL LAAHO YASMA-O’ TAHAAWORAKOMAA, INNAL LAAHA SAMEE-U’M BASEER.\nAllah has certainly heard the speech of her who pleads with you about her husband and complains to Allah. Allah hears the conversation between the two of you. Indeed Allah is all-hearing, all-seeing.\nاَلَّذِيْنَ يُظٰهِرُوْنَ مِنْكُمْ مِّنْ نِّسَآئِهِمْ مَّا هُنَّ اُمَّهٰتِهِمْؕ اِنْ اُمَّهٰتُهُمْ اِلَّا الّٰٓىِئْ وَلَدْنَهُمْؕ وَاِنَّهُمْ لَيَقُوْلُوْنَ مُنْكَرًا مِّنَ الْقَوْلِ وَزُوْرًاؕ وَ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ لَعَفُوٌّ غَفُوْرٌ‏(2)\nLAZEENA YOZAAHEROONA MINKUM MIN NESAAA-EHIM MAA HUNNA UMMAHAATEHIM, IN UMMAHAATOHUM ILLAL LAAA-EE WALADNAHUM, WA INNAHUM LAYAQOOLOONA MUNKARAM MENAL QAWLE WA ZOORAA, WA INNAL LAAHA LA-A’FUWWUN GHAFOOR.\nAs for those of you who repudiate their wives by zihar, they are not their mothers; their mothers are only those who bore them, and indeed they utter an outrage and a lie. Indeed Allah is all-excusing, all-forgiving.\nوَالَّذِيْنَ يُظٰهِرُوْنَ مِنْ نِّسَآئِهِمْ ثُمَّ يَعُوْدُوْنَ لِمَا قَالُوْا فَتَحْرِيْرُ رَقَبَةٍ مِّنْ قَبْلِ اَنْ يَّتَمَآسَّا ؕ ذٰ لِكُمْ تُوْعَظُوْنَ بِهٖ ؕ وَاللّٰهُ بِمَا تَعْمَلُوْنَ خَبِيْرٌ‏(3)\nWAL LAZEENA YOZAAHEROONA MIN NESAAA-EHIM SUMMA YA-O’ODOONA LEMAA QAALOO FA-TAHREERO RAQABATIM MIN QABLE AN-Y YATAMAASSAA, ZAALEKUM TOO-A’ZOONA BEH, WAL LAAHO BEMAA TA’MALOONA KHABEER.\nThose who repudiate their wives by zihar and then retract what they have said, shall set free a slave before they may touch each other. This you are advised [to carry out], and Allah is well aware of what you do.\nفَمَنْ لَّمْ يَجِدْ فَصِيَامُ شَهْرَيْنِ مُتَتَابِعَيْنِ مِنْ قَبْلِ اَنْ يَّتَمَآسَّاؕ فَمَنْ لَّمْ يَسْتَطِعْ فَاِطْعَامُ سِتِّيْنَ مِسْكِيْنًاؕ ذٰلِكَ لِتُؤْمِنُوْا بِاللّٰهِ وَرَسُوْلِهٖؕ وَتِلْكَ حُدُوْدُ اللّٰهِؕ وَلِلْكٰفِرِيْنَ عَذَابٌ اَلِیْمٌ‏(4)\nFAMAL LAM YAJID FA-SEYAAMO SHAHRAYNE MOTATAABE-A’YNE MIN QABLE AN-Y YATAMAASSAA, FAMAL LAM YASTATE’ FA-IT-A’AMO SITTEENA MISKEENAA, ZAALEKA LE-TOAMENOO BIL-LAAHE WA RASOOLEH, WA TILKA HODOODUL LAAH, WA LIL-KAAFEREENA A’ZAABUN ALEEM.\nHe who cannot afford [to free a slave] shall fast for two successive months before they may touch each other. If he cannot [do so], he shall feed sixty needy persons. This, that you may have faith in Allah and His Apostle. These are Allah’s bounds, and there is a painful punishment for the faithless.\nاِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ يُحَآدُّوْنَ اللّٰهَ وَرَسُوْلَهٗ كُبِتُوْا كَمَا كُبِتَ الَّذِيْنَ مِنْ قَبْلِهِمْ وَقَدْ اَنْزَلْنَاۤ اٰيٰتٍۢ بَيِّنٰتٍ ؕ وَ لِلْكٰفِرِيْنَ عَذَابٌ مُّهِيْنٌ ۚ‏(5)\nINNAL LAZEENA YOHAADDOONAL LAAHA WA RASOOLAHU KOBETOO KAMAA KOBETAL LAZEENA MIN QABLEHIM WA QAD ANZALNAA AAYAATIM BAYYENAAT, WA LIL-KAAFEREENA A’ZAABUM MOHEEN.\nIndeed those who oppose Allah and His Apostle will be subdued just as those who passed before them were subdued. We have certainly sent down manifest signs, and there is a humiliating punishment for the faithless.\nيَوْمَ يَبْعَثُهُمُ اللّٰهُ جَمِيْعًا فَيُنَبِّئُهُمْ بِمَا عَمِلُوْا ؕ اَحْصٰٮهُ اللّٰهُ وَنَسُوْهُ ؕ وَاللّٰهُ عَلٰى كُلِّ شَىْءٍ شَهِيْدٌ‏(6)\nYAWMA YAB-A’SOHOMUL LAAHO JAMEE-A’N FA-YONABBE-OHUM BEMAA A’MELOO, AHSAAHUL LAAHO WA NASOOH, WAL LAAHO A’LAA KULLE SHAY-IN SHAHEED.\nThe day when Allah will raise them all together, He will inform them about what they have done. Allah has kept account of it, while they have forgotten, and Allah is witness to all things.\nاَلَمْ تَرَ اَنَّ اللّٰهَ يَعْلَمُ مَا فِى السَّمٰوٰتِ وَمَا فِى الْاَرْضِؕ مَا يَكُوْنُ مِنْ نَّجْوٰى ثَلٰثَةٍ اِلَّا هُوَ رَابِعُهُمْ وَلَا خَمْسَةٍ اِلَّا هُوَ سَادِسُهُمْ وَلَاۤ اَدْنٰى مِنْ ذٰ لِكَ وَلَاۤ اَكْثَرَ اِلَّا هُوَ مَعَهُمْ اَيْنَ مَا كَانُوْاۚ ثُمَّ يُنَبِّئُهُمْ بِمَا عَمِلُوْا يَوْمَ الْقِيٰمَةِ ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ بِكُلِّ شَىْءٍ عَلِيْمٌ‏(7)\nALAM TARA ANNAL LAAHA YA’LAMO MAA FIS SAMAAWAATE WA MAA FIL ARZ, MAA YAKOONO MIN NAJWAA SALAASATIN ILLAA HOWA RAABE-O’HUM WA LAA KHAMSATIN ILLAA HOWA SAADESOHUM WA LAA ADNAA MIN ZAALEKA WA LAA AKSARA ILLAA HOWA MA-A’HUM AYNA MAA KAANOO, SUMMA YONABBE-OHUM BEMAA A’MELOO YAWMAL QEYAAMAH, INNAL LAAHA BE-KULLE SHAY-IN A’LEEM.\nHave you not regarded that Allah knows whatever there is in the heavens and whatever there is in the earth? There dost not takes place any secret talk among three, but He is their fourth [companion], nor among five but He is their sixth, nor when they are less than that or more but He is with them wherever they may be. Then He will inform them about what they have done on the Day of Resurrection. Indeed Allah has knowledge of all things.\nاَلَمْ تَرَ اِلَى الَّذِيْنَ نُهُوْا عَنِ النَّجْوٰى ثُمَّ يَعُوْدُوْنَ لِمَا نُهُوْا عَنْهُ وَيَتَنٰجَوْنَ بِالْاِثْمِ وَالْعُدْوَانِ وَمَعْصِيَتِ الرَّسُوْلِ وَاِذَا جَآءُوْكَ حَيَّوْكَ بِمَا لَمْ يُحَيِّكَ بِهِ اللّٰهُۙ وَيَقُوْلُوْنَ فِىْۤ اَنْفُسِهِمْ لَوْلَا يُعَذِّبُنَا اللّٰهُ بِمَا نَقُوْلُؕ حَسْبُهُمْ جَهَنَّمُۚ يَصْلَوْنَهَاۚ فَبِئْسَ الْمَصِيْرُ‏(8)\nALAM TARA ELAL LAZEENA NOHOO A’NIN NAJWAA SUMMA YA-O’ODOONA LEMAA NOHOO A’NHO WA YATANAAJAWNA BIL-ISME WAL U’DWAANE WA MA’SEYATIR RASOOL, WA EZAA JAAA-OOKA HAYYAWKA BEMAA LAM YOHAYYEKA BEHIL LAAHO, WA YAQOOLOONA FEE ANFOSEHIM LAWLAA YO-A’ZZEBONAL LAAHO BEMAA NAQOOL, HASBOHUM JAHANNAM, YASLAWNAHAA, FA-BEASAL MASEER.\nHave you not regarded those who were forbidden from secret talks but again resumed what they had been forbidden from, and hold secret talks [imbued] with sin and transgression and disobedience to the Apostle? And when they come to you they greet you with words with which Allah never greeted you, and they say to themselves, ‘Why does not Allah punish us for what we say?!’ Let hell suffice them: they shall enter it, and it is an evil destination!\nيٰۤاَيُّهَا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْۤا اِذَا تَنَاجَيْتُمْ فَلَا تَتَنَاجَوْا بِالْاِثْمِ وَالْعُدْوَانِ وَمَعْصِيَتِ الرَّسُوْلِ وَتَنَاجَوْا بِالْبِرِّ وَالتَّقْوٰىؕ وَاتَّقُوا اللّٰهَ الَّذِىْۤ اِلَيْهِ تُحْشَرُوْنَ‏(9)\nYAA AYYOHAL LAZEENA AAMANOO EZAA TANAAJAYTUM FALAA TATANAAJAW BIL-ISME WAL U’DWAANE WA MA’SEYATIR RASOOLE WA TANAAJAW BIL-BIRRE WAT TAQWAA, WAT TAQUL LAAHAL LAZEE ELAYHE TOHSHAROON.\nO you who have faith! When you converse secretly, do not hold private conversations [imbued] with sin and aggression and disobedience to the Apostle, but converse in [a spirit of] piety and Godfearing, and be wary of Allah toward whom you will be gathered.\nاِنَّمَا النَّجْوٰى مِنَ الشَّيْطٰنِ لِيَحْزُنَ الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا وَلَيْسَ بِضَآرِّهِمْ شَيْئًا اِلَّا بِاِذْنِ اللّٰهِؕ وَعَلَى اللّٰهِ فَلْيَتَوَكَّلِ الْمُؤْمِنُوْنَ‏(10)\nINNAMAN NAJWAA MENASH SHAYTAANE LE-YAHZONAL LAZEENA AAMANOO WA LAYSA BE-ZAARREHIM SHAY-AN ILLAA BE-IZNIL LAAH, WA A’LAL LAAHE FALYATAWAKKALIL MOAMENOON.\nIndeed [malicious] secret talks are from Satan, that he may upset the faithful, but he cannot harm them in any way except by Allah’s leave, and in Allah let all the faithful put their trust.\nيٰۤاَيُّهَا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْۤا اِذَا قِيْلَ لَكُمْ تَفَسَّحُوْا فِى الْمَجٰلِسِ فَافْسَحُوْا يَفْسَحِ اللّٰهُ لَكُمْ ۚ وَاِذَا قِيْلَ انْشُزُوْا فَانْشُزُوْا يَرْفَعِ اللّٰهُ الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا مِنْكُمْ ۙ وَالَّذِيْنَ اُوْتُوا الْعِلْمَ دَرَجٰتٍ ؕ وَاللّٰهُ بِمَا تَعْمَلُوْنَ خَبِيْرٌ‏(11)\nYAA AYYOHAL LAZEENA AAMANOO EZAA QEELA LAKUM TAFASSAHOO FIL MAJAALESE FAFSAHOO YAFSAHIL LAAHO LAKUM, WA EZAA QEELAN SHOZOO FANSHOZOO YARFA-I’L LAAHUL LAZEENA AAMANOO MINKUM, WAL LAZEENA OOTUL I’LMA DARAJAAT, WAL LAAHO BEMAA TA’MALOONA KHABEER.\nO you who have faith! When you are told, ‘Make room,’ in sittings, then do make room; Allah will make room for you. And when you are told, ‘Rise up!’ Do rise up. Allah will raise in rank those of you who have faith and those who have been given knowledge, and Allah is well aware of what you do.\nيٰۤاَيُّهَا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْۤا اِذَا نَاجَيْتُمُ الرَّسُوْلَ فَقَدِّمُوْا بَيْنَ يَدَىْ نَجْوٰٮكُمْ صَدَقَةً  ؕ ذٰ لِكَ خَيْرٌ لَّكُمْ وَاَطْهَرُ ؕ فَاِنْ لَّمْ تَجِدُوْا فَاِنَّ اللّٰهَ غَفُوْرٌ رَّحِيْمٌ‏(12)\nYAA AYYOHAL LAZEENA AAMANOO EZAA NAAJAYTOMUR RASOOLA FA-QADDEMOO BAYNA YADAY NAJWAAKUM SADAQAH, ZAALEKA KHAYRUL LAKUM WA ATHAR, FA-IL LAM TAJEDOO FA-INNAL LAAHA GHAFOORUR RAHEEM.\nO you who have faith! When you converse privately with the Apostle, offer a charity before your private talk. That is better for you and purer. But if you cannot afford [to make the offering], then Allah is indeed all-forgiving, all-merciful.\nءَاَشْفَقْتُمْ اَنْ تُقَدِّمُوْا بَيْنَ يَدَىْ نَجْوٰٮكُمْ صَدَقٰتٍ ؕ فَاِذْ لَمْ تَفْعَلُوْا وَتَابَ اللّٰهُ عَلَيْكُمْ فَاَقِيْمُوا الصَّلٰوةَ وَ اٰتُوا الزَّكٰوةَ وَاَطِيْعُوا اللّٰهَ وَرَسُوْلَهٗ ؕ وَاللّٰهُ خَبِيْرٌۢ بِمَا تَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(13)\nA-ASHFAQTUM AN TOQADDEMOO BAYNA YADAY NAJWAAKUM SADAQAAT, FA-IZ LAM TAF-A’LOO WA TAABAL LAAHO A’LAYKUM FA-AQEEMUS SALAATA WA AATUZ ZAKAATA WA ATEE-U’L LAAHA WA RASOOLAH, WAL LAAHO KHABEERUM BEMAA TA’MALOON.\nWere you dismayed by having to offer charities before your private talks? Since you did not do it, and Allah has excused you [for not be able to comply], now maintain the prayer and pay the zakat, and obey Allah and His Apostle. Allah is well aware of what you do.\nاَلَمْ تَرَ اِلَى الَّذِيْنَ تَوَلَّوْا قَوْمًا غَضِبَ اللّٰهُ عَلَيْهِمْؕ مَّا هُمْ مِّنْكُمْ وَلَا مِنْهُمْۙ وَيَحْلِفُوْنَ عَلَى الْكَذِبِ وَهُمْ يَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(14)\nALAM TARA ELAL LAZEENA TAWALLAW QAWMAN GHAZEBAL LAAHO A’LAYHIM, MAA HUM MINKUM WA LAA MINHUM, WA YAHLEFOONA A’LAL KAZEBE WA HUM YA’LAMOON.\nHave you not regarded those who befriend a people at whom Allah is wrathful? They neither belong to you, nor to them, and they swear false oaths [that they are with you] and they know.\nاَعَدَّ اللّٰهُ لَهُمْ عَذَابًا شَدِيْدًا ؕ اِنَّهُمْ سَآءَ مَا كَانُوْا يَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(15)\nA-A’DDAL LAAHO LAHUM A’ZAABAN SHADEEDAA, INNAHUM SAAA-A MAA KAANOO YA’MALOON.\nAllah has prepared a severe punishment for them. Evil indeed is what they used to do.\nاِتَّخَذُوْۤا اَيْمَانَهُمْ جُنَّةً فَصَدُّوْا عَنْ سَبِيْلِ اللّٰهِ فَلَهُمْ عَذَابٌ مُّهِيْنٌ‏(16)\nITTAKHAZOO AYMAANAHUM JUNNATAN FA-SADDOO A’N SABEELIL LAAHE FALAHUM A’ZAABUM MOHEEN.\nThey make a shield of their oaths and bar [people] from the way of Allah; so there is a humiliating punishment for them.\nلَنْ تُغْنِىَ عَنْهُمْ اَمْوَالُهُمْ وَلَاۤ اَوْلَادُهُمْ مِّنَ اللّٰهِ شَيْئًا ؕ اُولٰٓئِكَ اَصْحٰبُ النَّارِ ؕ هُمْ فِيْهَا خٰلِدُوْنَ‏(17)\nLAN TUGHNEYA A’NHUM AMWAALOHUM WA LAA AWLAADOHUM MENAL LAAHE SHAY-AA, OOLAAA-EKA ASHAABUN NAAR, HUM FEEHAA KHAALEDOON.\nTheir possessions and children will not avail them in any way against Allah. They shall be the inmates of the Fire and they shall remain in it [forever].\nيَوْمَ يَبْعَثُهُمُ اللّٰهُ جَمِيْعًا فَيَحْلِفُوْنَ لَهٗ كَمَا يَحْلِفُوْنَ لَكُمْ وَيَحْسَبُوْنَ اَنَّهُمْ عَلٰى شَىْءٍ ؕ اَلَاۤ اِنَّهُمْ هُمُ الْكٰذِبُوْنَ‏(18)\nYAWMA YAB-A’SOHOMUL LAAHO JAMEE-A’N FA-YAHLEFOONA LAHU KAMAA YAHLEFOONA LAKUM WA YAHSABOONA ANNAHUM A’LAA SHAY, ALAA INNAHUM HOMUL KAAZEBOON.\nThe day when Allah will raise them all together, they will swear to Him, just like they swear to you [now], supposing that they stand on something. Look! They are indeed liars!\nاِسْتَحْوَذَ عَلَيْهِمُ الشَّيْطٰنُ فَاَنْسٰٮهُمْ ذِكْرَ اللّٰهِؕ اُولٰٓئِكَ حِزْبُ الشَّيْطٰنِؕ اَلَاۤ اِنَّ حِزْبَ الشَّيْطٰنِ هُمُ الْخٰسِرُوْنَ‏(19)\nISTAHWAZA A’LAYHEMUSH SHAYTAANO FA-ANSAAHUM ZIKRAL LAAH, OOLAAA-EKA HIZBUSH SHAYTAAN, ALAA INNA HIZBASH SHAYTAANE HOMUL KHAASEROON.\nSatan has prevailed upon them, so he has caused them to forget the remembrance of Allah. They are Satan’s confederates. Look! Indeed, it is Satan’s confederates who are the losers!\nاِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ يُحَآدُّوْنَ اللّٰهَ وَرَسُوْلَهٗۤ اُولٰٓئِكَ فِى الْاَذَلِّيْنَ‏(20)\nINNAL LAZEENA YOHAADDOONAL LAAHA WA RASOOLAHU OOLAAA-EKA FIL AZALLEEN.\nIndeed those who oppose Allah and His Apostle—they will be among the most abased.\nكَتَبَ اللّٰهُ لَاَغْلِبَنَّ اَنَا وَرُسُلِىْؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ قَوِىٌّ عَزِيْزٌ‏(21)\nKATABAL LAAHO LA-AGHLEBANNA ANAA WA ROSOLEE, INNAL LAAHA QAWIYYUN A’ZEEZ.\nAllah has ordained: ‘I shall surely prevail, I and My apostles.’ Indeed Allah is all-strong, all-mighty.\nلَا تَجِدُ قَوْمًا يُّؤْمِنُوْنَ بِاللّٰهِ وَالْيَوْمِ الْاٰخِرِ يُوَآدُّوْنَ مَنْ حَآدَّ اللّٰهَ وَرَسُوْلَهٗ وَلَوْ كَانُوْۤا اٰبَآءَهُمْ اَوْ اَبْنَآءَهُمْ اَوْ اِخْوَانَهُمْ اَوْ عَشِيْرَتَهُمْؕ اُولٰٓئِكَ كَتَبَ فِىْ قُلُوْبِهِمُ الْاِيْمَانَ وَاَيَّدَهُمْ بِرُوْحٍ مِّنْهُ ؕ وَيُدْخِلُهُمْ جَنّٰتٍ تَجْرِىْ مِنْ تَحْتِهَا الْاَنْهٰرُ خٰلِدِيْنَ فِيْهَا ؕ رَضِىَ اللّٰهُ عَنْهُمْ وَرَضُوْا عَنْهُ ؕ اُولٰٓئِكَ حِزْبُ اللّٰهِ ؕ اَلَاۤ اِنَّ حِزْبَ اللّٰهِ هُمُ الْمُفْلِحُوْنَ‏(22)\nLAA TAJEDO QAWMAN-Y YOAMENOONA BIL-LAAHE WAL YAWMIL AAKHERE YOWAADDOONA MAN HAADDAL LAAHA WA RASOOLAHU WA LAW KAANOO AABAAA-AHUM AW ABNAAA-AHUM AW IKHWAANAHUM AW A’SHEERATAHUM, OOLAAA-EKA KATABA FEE QOLOOBEHEMUL EEMAANA WA AYYADAHUM BE-ROOHIM MINH, WA YUDKHELOHUM JANNAATIN TAJREE MIN TAHTEHAL ANHAARO KHAALEDEENA FEEHAA, RAZEYAL LAAHO A’NHUM WA RAZOO A’NH, OOLAAA-EKA HIZBUL LAAH, ALAA INNA HIZBAL LAAHE HOMUL MUFLEHOON.\nYou will not find a people believing in Allah and the Last Day endearing those who oppose Allah and His Apostle even though they were their own parents, or children, or brothers, or kinsfolk. [For] such, He has written faith into their hearts and strengthened them with a spirit from Him. He will admit them into gardens with streams running in them, to remain in them [forever], Allah is pleased with them, and they are pleased with Him. They are Allah’s confederates. Look! The confederates of Allah are indeed felicitous!",
  "merits": "Surah Mujaadelah (The Pleading One)\nThere are 22 verses in this Surah and it was revealed in Madinah. The Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) said that the one who recites this Surah will be from among the thankful servants of Allah (s.w.t.) on the Day of Judgement. If Surah al-Mujaadelah is recited near a sick person, or worn by the sick person as a talisman, he will be cured of his illness. If recited on anything that has been buried in the ground, it will remain protected until the person himself removes it.\nReciting this Surah brings a feeling of ease to a restless person. Constant recitation also protects one from thieves. Imam Ja’far al-Sadiq (a.s.) has said that recitation of this Surah keeps one safe from the evil designs of Jinn and men. If recited on dust or sand and then thrown towards the enemy, he is easily overcome."
